Z||000000||kinboyatuwo||07-04-2001||01:11 AM||||guys, my car will be sitting for a bit<BR>how long will cause specific prob, will start her weekly, anything else?<BR>thanks<BR>kin<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/b4lower50.jpg"> <BR>"Friends don't let friends drive four doors."<P>87 Duke, 235,000km||||reg||1
Z||000001||Steve Normington||07-04-2001||01:19 AM||||Jack it up and rest in on the frame rails so the tires don't get a flat spot. Change the oil, coolant, and grease all the joints. Also, when you start it, make sure it gets up to full operating temperature to evaporate any water in the oil. Fill the fuel tank completely full. When you start it, run it through forward and reverse gears and operate the hand and foot brakes. Finally, put some moth balls or Bounce™ dryer sheets in the various openings to discourage critters.||||reg||1
